  "details": "When I put on a Generic avatar with a custom Action layer, I see the Action pose before any Playable Layer Control runs. Remote player can see it too. My Humanoid version starts in the Base pose.\n\nHow to check\n\n* Put on https://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_3140df12-9c00-4045-a40d-25726fa4e3e8\n\n* In Desktop, press F5 to see the result\n\nI expected Base to show first because the docs say Action starts at zero weight. Is the Generic behavior intended? If it is, could the docs mention the difference? https://creators.vrchat.com/avatars/playable-layers/#action\n\nHow to reproduce the avatar\n\n* Start with a Generic rig and a VRC Avatar Descriptor. Add a visible cube as a child of the avatar root.\n\n* Create two Animator Controllers, each with a single default state. In the Base controller, use a clip that holds the cube low. In the Action controller, use a clip that holds the same cube high. Animate the cube’s local position in both clips.\n\n* In the descriptor, customize Playable Layers and assign the controllers to Base and Action.\n\n* Upload and wear the avatar. The cube appears high in the Action pose.",
